<title>USA: Mobil Corp unit sells Egypt concessions.</title>
<headline>Mobil Corp unit sells Egypt concessions.</headline>
<dateline>FAIRFAX, Va. 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mobil Corp said Tuesday that Mobil Exploration Egypt Inc, its wholly owned subsidiary, has sold non-operated exploration concessions in Egypt's western desert to the Apache Corp.</p>
<p>The financial terms were not disclosed for the deal, which took effect last Thursday and has been approved by the Egyptian Government.</p>
<p>The concessions included are the East Bahariya (operated by Repsol ; Mobil's interest was 50 percent); West Mediterreanean Block 1 (operated by Repsol; Mobil's interest was 33 percent) and NE Abu Gharadig (operated by Royal Dutch Shell Group; Mobil's interest was 24 percent).</p>
</text>
